 ## Live Game Channels & Frontend
 
-- **Security**: While `status == "question_open"`, player HTML (`GET /play/:code`), JSON (`GET /play/:code/state`, `POST /play/:code/answer`), and shared WebSocket broadcasts (`game:<id>:players`) strictly omit `correct` flags; points/places are strictly omitted until `finished`. `GameModeratorChannel` requires a `MessageVerifier`-signed `moderator_token` issued only on `/moderate` pages.
+- **Security**: While `status == "question_open"`, player HTML (`GET /play/:code`), JSON (`GET /play/:code/state`, `POST /play/:code/answer`), and shared WebSocket broadcasts (`game:<id>:players`) strictly omit `correct` flags and timer fields; points/places are strictly omitted until `finished`. `GameModeratorChannel` requires a `MessageVerifier`-signed `moderator_token` issued only on `/moderate` pages.
 - **QR Code**: Generated server-side via `rqrcode` (`ApplicationHelper#render_qr_svg`) as a self-contained inline `<svg>` encoding the full join URL (`http://<host>:<port>/play/<CODE>`).
 - **Conference Wi-Fi Resilience**: Stimulus controllers (`moderator-game` and `play-game`) combine live Action Cable WebSocket streams with monotonic `state_version` guards, serialized moderator action queues (`this.actionQueue`), automatic state resync on reconnect/`visibilitychange`/`online`/`pageshow`, answer `fetch` retry with `AbortController`, and a 2s `/state` fallback poll whenever the WebSocket is disconnected.
